                    <div class="n2-ss-static-slide n2-ow"><div class="n2-ss-layer n2-ow n-uc-eoYZHdqsfiYZ" data-sstype="slide" data-pm="default"><div class="n2-ss-layer n2-ow n-uc-82bxcDGDp8G6" data-pm="default" data-sstype="content" data-hasbackground="0"><div class="n2-ss-section-main-content n2-ss-layer-with-background n2-ss-layer-content n2-ow n-uc-82bxcDGDp8G6-inner"><div class="n2-ss-layer n2-ow n2-ss-layer--block n2-ss-has-self-align n-uc-U66ZPGkhKFwR" data-pm="normal" data-sstype="row"><div class="n2-ss-layer-row n2-ss-layer-with-background n-uc-U66ZPGkhKFwR-inner"><div class="n2-ss-layer-row-inner "><div class="n2-ss-layer n2-ow n-uc-1nOevI8FV5lX" data-pm="default" data-sstype="col"><div class="n2-ss-layer-col n2-ss-layer-with-background n2-ss-layer-content n-uc-1nOevI8FV5lX-inner"><div class="n2-ss-layer n2-ow n-uc-YmVZtwrfgK7C" data-pm="normal" data-sstype="layer"><div class=" n2-ss-item-image-content n2-ss-item-content n2-ow-all"><img decoding="async" id="n2-ss-4item1" alt="" class="skip-lazy" loading="lazy" width="415" height="95" data-skip-lazy="1" src="//gemstat.org/wp-content/uploads/2019/12/Logo_GEMS_Water_4c_2019.png" /></div></div><div class="n2-ss-layer n2-ow n-uc-AQBX21xsv1te" data-pm="normal" data-sstype="layer"><div class="n2-ss-item-content n2-ss-text n2-ow-all"><div class=""><p class="n2-font-8e7b0b7aca5ab9b4a5197c557f1c3a7b-paragraph   ">The Global Freshwater Quality Database GEMStat provides scientifically-sound data and information on the state and trend of global inland water quality. As operational part of the GEMS/Water Programme of the United Nations Environment Programme (UNEP), GEMStat is hosted by the GEMS/Water Data Centre (GWDC) within the International Centre for Water Resources and Global Change (ICWRGC) in Koblenz, Germany.</p>
