          <div class="hover-wrap-inner">
            <a href="https://gemstat.org/projects/geo/" target="_self" class="">
              <img decoding="async" class="img-with-animation skip-lazy" data-delay="0" height="1215" width="2560" data-animation="fade-in" src="https://gemstat.org/wp-content/uploads/2025/07/aquawatch_colour_logo_small-scaled.png" alt="Logo GEO Aquawatch" srcset="https://gemstat.org/wp-content/uploads/2025/07/aquawatch_colour_logo_small-scaled.png 2560w, https://gemstat.org/wp-content/uploads/2025/07/aquawatch_colour_logo_small-300x142.png 300w, https://gemstat.org/wp-content/uploads/2025/07/aquawatch_colour_logo_small-1024x486.png 1024w, https://gemstat.org/wp-content/uploads/2025/07/aquawatch_colour_logo_small-768x364.png 768w, https://gemstat.org/wp-content/uploads/2025/07/aquawatch_colour_logo_small-1536x729.png 1536w, https://gemstat.org/wp-content/uploads/2025/07/aquawatch_colour_logo_small-2048x972.png 2048w" sizes="(max-width: 2560px) 100vw, 2560px" />
            </a>
          </div>
        </div>
        
      </div>
      </div><h3 style="color: #444444;text-align: left" class="vc_custom_heading vc_do_custom_heading vc_custom_1767626440755" ><a href="https://gemstat.org/projects/geo/" title="GEO Aquawatch">GEO Aquawatch</a></h3>
<div class="wpb_text_column wpb_content_element " >
	<p>Earth observation methodology possesses great potential to support water quality monitoring programmes, particularly in remote and inaccessible areas. However, thorough calibration of the associated algorithms is required to ensure reliable observations. GEO Aquawatch is an initiative which aims to establish and develop global applications of water quality data based on earth observation.</p>
</div>



<a class="nectar-button small regular accent-color  regular-button"  role="button" style="margin-top: 15px; "  href="https://gemstat.org/projects/geo/" data-color-override="false" data-hover-color-override="false" data-hover-text-color-override="#fff"><span>READ MORE</span></a>
		</div> 
	</div>
	</div> 
</div></div>
			</div> 
		</div>
	</div> 

	<div  class="vc_col-sm-3 wpb_column column_container vc_column_container col padding-1-percent inherit_tablet inherit_phone "  data-border-radius="3px" data-border-animation="" data-border-animation-delay="" data-border-width="1px" data-border-style="solid" data-border-color="#305DA8" data-padding-pos="all" data-has-bg-color="false" data-bg-color="" data-bg-opacity="1" data-animation="" data-delay="0" >
		<div class="vc_column-inner" style="border: 1px solid #305DA8;">
			<div class="wpb_wrapper">
				<div id="fws_6a5c7ede229d3" data-midnight="" data-column-margin="default" class="wpb_row vc_row-fluid vc_row inner_row vc_row-o-equal-height vc_row-flex vc_row-o-content-middle"  style=""><div class="row-bg-wrap"> <div class="row-bg" ></div> </div><div class="row_col_wrap_12_inner col span_12  left">
	<div  class="vc_col-sm-12 wpb_column column_container vc_column_container col child_column no-extra-padding inherit_tablet inherit_phone flex_gap_desktop_10px "   data-padding-pos="all" data-has-bg-color="false" data-bg-color="" data-bg-opacity="1" data-animation="" data-delay="0" >
		<div class="vc_column-inner" >
		<div class="wpb_wrapper">
			<div class="img-with-aniamtion-wrap " data-max-width="100%" data-max-width-mobile="default" data-shadow="none" data-animation="fade-in"  style="margin-top: 5%; margin-right: 10%; ">
      <div class="inner">
        <div class="hover-wrap"> 
          <div class="hover-wrap-inner">
            <a href="https://gemstat.org/projects/ogc-wqie/" target="_self" class="">
              <img decoding="async" class="img-with-animation skip-lazy" data-delay="0" height="840" width="2560" data-animation="fade-in" src="https://gemstat.org/wp-content/uploads/2025/07/Open_Geospatial_Consortium_logo-scaled.png" alt="Logo of the Open Geospatial Consortium" srcset="https://gemstat.org/wp-content/uploads/2025/07/Open_Geospatial_Consortium_logo-scaled.png 2560w, https://gemstat.org/wp-content/uploads/2025/07/Open_Geospatial_Consortium_logo-300x98.png 300w, https://gemstat.org/wp-content/uploads/2025/07/Open_Geospatial_Consortium_logo-1024x336.png 1024w, https://gemstat.org/wp-content/uploads/2025/07/Open_Geospatial_Consortium_logo-768x252.png 768w, https://gemstat.org/wp-content/uploads/2025/07/Open_Geospatial_Consortium_logo-1536x504.png 1536w, https://gemstat.org/wp-content/uploads/2025/07/Open_Geospatial_Consortium_logo-2048x672.png 2048w" sizes="(max-width: 2560px) 100vw, 2560px" />
            </a>
          </div>
        </div>
        
      </div>
      </div><h3 style="color: #444444;text-align: left" class="vc_custom_heading vc_do_custom_heading vc_custom_1767626390379" ><a href="https://gemstat.org/projects/ogc-wqie/" title="OGC Water Quality Interoperability Experiment">OGC Water Quality Interoperability Experiment</a></h3>
<div class="wpb_text_column wpb_content_element " >
	<p>Water quality monitoring data are continuously collected in local, national and multinational databases, which need to be linked to provide information on a global scale. The OGC Water Quality Interoperability Experiment is testing the interoperability and connectivity of existing water quality platforms, using a framework developed from the OGC WaterML suite of standards, the OGC SensorThings API and the OGC standard on Observations, Measurements and Sample.</p>
</div>



<a class="nectar-button small regular accent-color  regular-button"  role="button" style="margin-top: 15px; "  href="https://gemstat.org/projects/ogc-wqie/" data-color-override="false" data-hover-color-override="false" data-hover-text-color-override="#fff"><span>READ MORE</span></a>
		</div> 
	</div>
	</div> 
</div></div>
			</div> 
		</div>
	</div> 

